{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Patel. I’ll be your doctor during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve been really nauseous since this morning and I’ve thrown up a few times. I also have this cramping pain in my stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, diarrhea, or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or chest pain. I had one loose stool yesterday, but that’s it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You have type 1 diabetes—have you been able to keep your insulin up with not eating much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying, but I’m scared of going low. My sugars have been all over the place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll give you IV fluids and monitor your glucose closely. We also need to check for signs of ketoacidosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. Is that what’s happening again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your initial labs show a slightly low bicarbonate but no big acid buildup yet. We’ll keep watching. You’re not in full DKA, but we’re seeing early signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not full DKA, but close?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2123-02-22 01:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re catching it early. IV fluids and careful insulin will help reverse it. We’ll also give you something for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling? Any vomiting since last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous. I threw up once after coughing, but not on my own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s better than constant vomiting. Your labs this morning show your bicarbonate dropped to 17 and anion gap went up to 15—still mild, but we’re treating it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not severe, but it means your body is starting to burn fat for fuel. We’re correcting it with fluids and adjusting your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been compliant with my insulin, I swear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2123-02-22 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I believe you. Sometimes illness alone can throw things off, even if you’re doing everything right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to start you on a liquid diet to see if you can keep things down. Still no fever or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just the nausea and stomach cramps. Oh, and my back’s been killing me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned that. Where exactly is the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Middle of my back, on the left side. It’s been bad for years, ever since my car accident."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get an X-ray to make sure nothing’s changed. For now, we can try some acetaminophen and a lidocaine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually take oxycodone, but I ran out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2123-02-22 14:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re avoiding narcotics in the hospital because they can worsen nausea and aren’t great for long-term back pain. Let’s try safer options first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2123-02-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your back X-ray came back. Good news—it’s normal. No fractures or changes from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2123-02-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s wrong with my spine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2123-02-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Structurally, no. The pain is likely muscular or related to old injury. We’ll keep using heat and the lidocaine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2123-02-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It helps a little, but I still need something stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2123-02-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll focus on non-narcotic options. Long-term, narcotics can make pain worse and aren’t safe with your other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2123-02-23 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your nausea is improving. You kept down apple juice and broth. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2123-02-23 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel queasy, but not like yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2123-02-23 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think this is viral gastroenteritis—your labs don’t show infection, and you don’t have fever. It should pass in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2123-02-23 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could it be gastroparesis? I’ve heard that happens with diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2123-02-23 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We considered that, but gastroparesis usually doesn’t come on suddenly, and you had diarrhea, which is less common with it. But you should get tested later if symptoms return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2123-02-23 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your blood work is improving. Bicarbonate is back to 20, no anion gap. You’re out of the early DKA phase."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! Does that mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. You need to keep down solid food and stay stable. We’ll try a soft diet today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my insulin? I’ve been so confused with the doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We lowered your Lantus to 15 units because you were having lows—down to 40s. You responded well to juice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hate going low. It scares me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’ll send you home with clear instructions: 15 units tonight, then back to 31 tomorrow when you’re eating normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sliding scale?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2123-02-24 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using Humalog as before, but don’t take more than 5 units at night. We’re keeping that limit to prevent lows."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2123-02-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well today—kept down toast and applesauce. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2123-02-24 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2123-02-24 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue lisinopril, ezetimibe, aspirin, and your insulin. We’re adding compazine for nausea and ranitidine for heartburn."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2123-02-24 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And for my back pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2123-02-24 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Acetaminophen and lidocaine patches. Use the patch for 12 hours, then off for 12. No narcotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2123-02-24 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess I’ll have to manage without them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. You’ve kept down a full meal. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When should I worry and come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your blood sugar goes below 60 or above 350, or if you can’t keep food or liquids down. Also, chest pain or trouble breathing—go straight to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your primary doctor soon. We tried to schedule a mental health visit, but you’ve missed a few in the past?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know… anxiety makes it hard. But I’ll try this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. Managing stress helps your diabetes too. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel a lot better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2123-02-25 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The nurse will go over your prescriptions and discharge instructions now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2123-02-22 01:25:00",
    "admission_end": "2123-02-25 15:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and epigastric pain. She developed early signs of diabetic ketoacidosis with a falling bicarbonate and rising anion gap, which resolved with IV fluids and insulin adjustment. Despite improvement in metabolic parameters, nausea persisted, and she was diagnosed with viral gastroenteritis. She tolerated a gradual return to oral intake and was stabilized on insulin with a temporary reduction in Lantus due to hypoglycemia. Chronic low back pain was evaluated with a normal lumbar spine X-ray; treatment shifted to non-narcotic methods including acetaminophen and lidocaine patches. She was discharged home in stable condition with new prescriptions for compazine and ranitidine, clear insulin instructions, and follow-up plans.",
    "problems": [
      "Intestinal infection due to other organism, not elsewhere classified",
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Lumbago",
      "Other chronic pain"
    ]
  }
}
